collides elsewhere. Explicit negative examples (length-hash collisions and
hiding-at-equality refutations) intentionally exhibit collisions; they are not
binding claims and now name their exhibited pair too.

Critique: larger types expose the actual comparison trace, and explicit witnesses
make omission statements less convenient to call. That cost buys an inspectable
claim whose escape cannot be supplied by an unrelated collision.
Meta-critique: a count of scoped predicates alone does not establish nonvacuity.
The check must be paired with finite-width separation witnesses and a real
dropped-list mutant of each theorem. The mutation is a proved weakening of the
actual declaration and must produce a checked RED, not a scripted error string.
No digest, wire encoding, verification verdict or refusal policy changes.

Additional PRICE PREMISES after the disjunct read: DomainEpoch.Example.committed_cells_agree_instance gains a candidate vector family and its per-tick Opens evidence. Its former first disjunct compared one expression to itself and was provable by reflexivity; merely scoping the second disjunct would leave the example vacuous. The replacement compares the honest vectors with the supplied candidate. No other landed theorem gains a hypothesis in this adjustment.

Regression inventory: scripts/gates/scoped-collision-sites.tsv names 47 result
reductions/refutations and the WorldRoot separation-premise consumer. Verify's
Collision*Teeth modules compile the positive checks and kernel proofs of finite
instances. The result mutation uses the actual theorem to derive the old unbounded
conclusion; the premise mutation derives the old global-separation version from
local separation contravariantly. Each mutant must compile with the check absent
and fail with the check present. The runner captures the actual RED lines, rejects
other errors, and rejects a missing source assertion against the fixed inventory.
This is a regression check for the identified shape, not a general vacuity solver.

Finite instances include 256-bit node hashes that collide outside a successful
trie/range/log comparison, an accepted deployed hashEq opening, the concrete epoch
omission vector, nonempty deployed-index openings, and two distinct worlds with
equal roots whose node escape is false (their system-root collision explains the
equality). The receipt-framing model uses the same byte-input builders with a
256-bit-range hash separating the actual key/leaf inputs; it is explicitly a model,
not a claim that cSHAKE is injective. Literal deployed cSHAKE computation is not a
premise of the proof or a substitute for these bounded comparison statements.

## Coverage repair preceding signature migration

The existing ObjectiveProofs manifest omitted Theory.ObjectiveBendDigest and
Kernel.SealedMarket. Import both into ObjectiveProofs and include the digest in
the Mathlib-free partition. Capture the old declarations from the immutable
334316df warm oleans before recording their RESTATED events. The coverage
commit adds their original contracts; subsequent site commits replace them.
No floor or existing pin is relaxed. PRICE PREMISES for this coverage change:
none. Critique: extra coverage increases the scan surface. Meta-critique: an
untracked proof would make a purported complete restatement audit misleading.

The exact existing declarations with newly exposed arguments or evidence are:
